component SigilProjectionStore {
  goal {
    Publish disposable source-bound assertions without accepting stale or
    out-of-order reconstruction as current evidence.
  }

  interface {
    DisposableCleanup {
      Clean only generated worlds while holding the same exclusive writer lock.
      Recover even from a malformed index without interpreting its contents.
      Remove symlink artifacts themselves without following their targets.
      Keep the lock inode in place so cleanup cannot split concurrent writers.
      Preserve authored sources, workspace configuration and external job inputs.
    }

    ImplementationCommands {
      Prepare exactly one copied source file, fixed ontology and identity-only
      catalog for the worker. Keep its job descriptor with the external caller.
      Require current non-Disjoint Design and validate all catalog references
      before ingesting Implementation. Accept an explicit source selection for
      stale inspection and comparison. Compile each world independently, then
      compare Design obligations with Implementation closure in the fixed matcher.
      Completed Closed is green and Converged is yellow with warnings; both exit
      zero. Drift is red and exits one. Apply this mapping to compile
      implementation and compare. Missing current Design catalog leaves
      comparison unavailable, exits three, and never reports Drift.
    }

    CurrentImplementation {
      Select arbitrary-language source files and assemble only fresh indexed
      assertions against the current frozen Design catalog. Validate resource
      identity again on reading and enforce aggregate assertion limits before
      closure. Keep the catalog out of Implementation evidence.
      Saturate in an independent EGraph and identify the captured selection,
      catalog and assertion contents. Missing sources and completed empty facts
      remain distinct. Explicit empty selection is visible in the report.
    }

    DesignCommands {
      Expose prepare, ingest, stale and compile for Design and entities for its
      catalog. Accept an explicit frontend bundle and workspace root. Preparation
      writes only bound Design context, fixed ontology, a job descriptor and a
      artifact-evidence template into a new caller-selected directory;
      refuse to overwrite existing directories. The template binds its preparation
      and job references, and makes the required final pending attempt shape
      explicit without supplying worker, ingest, Turtle or result evidence.
      Ingestion checks the job source and current inputs before publication.
      Compile Design exits zero for Coherent (green) or Loose (yellow with
      warnings), and one only for Disjoint (red). Invalid options exit two;
      operational failure without a completed semantic result exits three.
      Inspection exits are command-specific: stale returns one for nonfresh
      sources, and entities returns one when no current catalog is available.
      Neither inspection exit is a semantic color.
      No provider, model or automatic repair options exist.
    }

    CurrentDesign {
      Assemble fresh source projections against a recaptured frontend snapshot.
      Add only structural type and label facts plus required unit inventory from
      the frontend. Missing projections leave Design Loose unless fresh facts
      already establish Disjoint. Frontend errors produce no completed verdict.
      Validate the complete identity set before freezing a current catalog.
      Reports identify captured inputs, projection contents and compiled kernel.
      Prepare Design context only from its bound source and dependency closure.
    }

    ProjectionPublication {
      Capture the expected per-source generation before reconstruction.
      Under one OS file lock, compare the prepared binding and generation with
      current inputs and recheck source and Design dependency bytes. Publish
      bounded data-only assertions by temporary-file replacement, then atomically
      replace the index that binds their checksum to inputs and generation.
      Reject duplicate jobs and changed source, catalog or format inputs.
      Publication tokens cannot repeat after cache deletion and reconstruction;
      an old job cannot regain authority when disposable generations restart.
      Keep scheduling and workers outside the store. At acceptance, persist an
      immutable versioned artifact-evidence record supplied by the external
      subagent: source binding, preparation and job references, native job
      fingerprint, worker process record, ingest command, every Turtle/result
      attempt, projection path and publication generation. This record is
      evidence linkage, not model data,
      a task ledger or a worker registry. Ingest rejects an incomplete evidence
      manifest when the caller asks for native evidence recording.
    }

    NativeArtifactEvidence {
      Accept an optional artifact-evidence manifest alongside a matching ingest
      job. Require the final pending attempt to name the submitted Turtle with
      exit null; native ingest writes its actual accepted exit zero. Preserve
      earlier rejected attempts with their observed exits without interpreting
      their text.

      Prepare emits a structurally valid template with exactly the manifest
      fields, one pending attempt with `exit: null`, and nonempty replacement
      references. A worker replaces those placeholder references, records each
      rejected attempt with its numeric exit, and keeps exactly one final pending
      attempt before ingest. Native diagnostics show the same minimal JSON shape.
      Bind the record to the accepted source fingerprint, generation and exact
      projection key. Expose every fresh source through projection index and
      expanded-world reports: complete records carry their links, while a null
      artifact explicitly identifies a projection that predates native evidence.
      A fresh process can therefore distinguish incomplete evidence without a
      temporary tracker. Existing entries without a record remain semantically
      readable but are incomplete evidence.
    }

    BindingHistory {
      Retain accepted projections for distinct semantic bindings of the same
      source in the disposable world store. Keep one current source-path
      publication and address superseded projections by their complete binding
      fingerprint, including the Implementation Design-catalog identity.
      Reuse a retained projection only when its complete binding is fresh for the
      current operation. Do not key this cache by request item, task, worker or
      scope identity, and do not turn it into a history or workflow ledger.
    }

    IndexedAssembly {
      Mirror normalized source paths with their original extensions plus egg.
      Load only index-selected assertions with matching complete input bindings
      and checksums. Parse them as restricted data. Missing, stale, corrupt,
      deleted and unindexed objects contribute no current facts.
      Bound index and assertion bytes separately. Refuse path traversal,
      symlinked artifact paths and malformed index metadata.
      A busy writer lock is an operational failure, never a semantic result.
    }
  }
}
